**suggestion:** Prefer a driver-standard logging mechanism over fprintf(stderr) for this warning.

Direct stderr logging from a driver can be noisy in multi-context apps and bypasses existing debug/logging controls. Please use the standard Mesa/r300 logging helper (e.g., the usual debug/warning macro) so this message respects configured verbosity and stays consistent with other driver diagnostics.

```suggestion
    /* A 65536-vertex draw with no alt support shifts to 0 in the count field
     * and underflows the kernel CS validator; refuse it rather than emit a
     * malformed IB that corrupts driver state. */
    if (!alt_num_verts && count > 65535) {
        debug_printf("r300: SWTCL draw of %u vertices exceeds the 16-bit "
                     "VAP count limit on a non-r5xx part; skipping.\n", count);
        return;
    }
