**suggestion (bug_risk):** Consider also treating VIEWPORT_WITH_COUNT / SCISSOR_WITH_COUNT as dynamic viewport/scissor state.

Right now `dynamic_viewport` / `dynamic_scissor` only react to `VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VIEWPORT` and `VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_SCISSOR`. For pipelines using `VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VIEWPORT_WITH_COUNT` or `VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_SCISSOR_WITH_COUNT`, these flags stay `false`, so later code may incorrectly treat `pViewportState` as statically valid and read from it, even though the spec allows that state to be ignored/garbage. Please extend this switch to handle the `*_WITH_COUNT` variants and set the corresponding booleans to avoid reading unused/invalid viewport state.

```suggestion
   bool dynamic_viewport = false;
   bool dynamic_scissor = false;
   bool dynamic_raster_discard = false;
   if (info->pDynamicState) {
      for (uint32_t d = 0; d < info->pDynamicState->dynamicStateCount; d++) {
         switch (info->pDynamicState->pDynamicStates[d]) {
         case VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VIEWPORT:
         case VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VIEWPORT_WITH_COUNT:
            dynamic_viewport = true;
            break;
         case VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_SCISSOR:
         case VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_SCISSOR_WITH_COUNT:
            dynamic_scissor = true;
            break;
         case VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_RASTERIZER_DISCARD_ENABLE:
            dynamic_raster_discard = true;
            break;
         default:
            break;
         }
      }
   }
```

**suggestion:** Clear path ignores VkImageSubresourceRange and always clears the whole image.

This helper currently disregards the VkImageSubresourceRange from r300vk_cmd_clear_color_image and always clears the full image. That matches the current single-mip, single-layer assumption, but any partial range (subset of mips/layers) will still result in a full clear. To avoid latent bugs if images are extended beyond single mip/layer, consider asserting that the range covers the full image (aspectMask/color only, baseMipLevel == 0, levelCount == 1, etc.).

Suggested implementation:

```c
   /* For now we only support full-image color clears. Assert that the
    * provided subresource range matches the whole image, and covers
    * exactly one mip level and all array layers. */
   assert(range->aspectMask == VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_COLOR_BIT);
   assert(range->baseMipLevel == 0);
   assert(range->levelCount == 1);
   assert(range->baseArrayLayer == 0);
   /* If the image is single-layer, this will typically be 1. For array/cubemap
    * images, this should match the image's total layer count. */
   assert(range->layerCount == img->info.array_size);

   const unsigned bpp = util_format_get_blocksize(dst_img->resource->format);

```

1. Update the `r300vk_clear_color_image` helper signature to take a `const VkImageSubresourceRange *range` parameter, e.g.:
   `static bool r300vk_clear_color_image(struct r300vk_device *device, const struct r300vk_image *img, const VkClearColorValue *color, const VkImageSubresourceRange *range)`.
2. Update all call sites (at least `r300vk_cmd_clear_color_image`) to pass the `VkImageSubresourceRange` they receive from the Vulkan command into this helper.
3. Ensure `img->info.array_size` (or equivalent) is the correct field for the total number of array layers; if the field name differs, adjust the assertion accordingly.
4. If this file does not already include `<assert.h>`, add `#include <assert.h>` near the other standard-library includes.
